2019,P2,4,ANALYTICAL GEOMETRY,AGEO,,,,,,,suggestions,DBE diagnostic,567,558,True,"(d) NATIONAL SENIOR CERTIFICATE DIAGNOSTIC REPORT PART 1 | 2019 197 Although learners determine the equation of a straight line from Grade 9, they should be reminded that the minimum requirements to determine the equation of a straight line is the gradient of the line and the coordinates of one point through which the line passes. Teachers should ensure that they expose learners to assessments that integrate Analytical Geometry and Euclidean Geometry. Learners must also be exposed to higher-order questions in class and in school-based assessment tasks."
